 $70,000 - $80,000 a year your job is to turn chicken shit into chicken salad. every day.it sucks but it might make you a lot of money. or it might now, depends how things go. who we are we run multiple businesses: federal healthcare staffing, medical transportation, acquisitions. there’s a lot going on, things move fast, and some of it is a mess. that’s where you come in. the job your title is executer because your job is to execute . you work directly with the ceo, and you do what needs to be done. stalled project? get it moving. broken process? fix it. vendor ghosting us? track them down. proposal due tomorrow and nobody’s started? guess who’s starting. your job is to turn chicken shit into chicken salad. every day. what you’ll actually do take shit that’s broken and fix it take shit that’s stuck and move it take shit that’s an idea and make it real be the ceo’s right hand across ops, bd, finance, admin, whatever chase people down until things are handled write docs, build trackers, put sops together, research problems, find answers juggle 10 things and drop none of them come back with “it’s done,” not “what should i do?” be prepared to fail and then immediately forget and restart you’re our person if you finish what you start, every time you don’t need hand-holding. you figure it out (chicken shit into chicken salad). chaos doesn’t scare you. it’s tuesday. you tell it straight and flag problems before they blow up you’re organized enough that nothing falls through the cracks you’re not our person if you need a detailed playbook for everything you say “that’s not my job” you confuse being busy with getting results you need to be managed to stay productive requirements ideally you had danced with the devil and won proof you’ve owned problems and solved them can write clearly and communicate like an adult comfortable with google workspace/m365, spreadsheets, and project tools self-driven in a remote setup and reachable during hours (chicken shit into chicken salad) bonus points government contracting, healthcare, staffing, or transportation experience must be good with technology you use ai tools to move faster why this job if you got down this far in the jd and still want to read more this section is irrelevant &nbsp; 
